# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env` on its own matched only that exact name. A `.env.local` or a `.env.production`
# would have been committed by the next `git add -A`, which is how this goes wrong: not
# by adding a secret on purpose, but by adding a file nobody thought was one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Keystores and their passwords, wherever they are put. `.wrasse/` covers today's layout
# and these cover a copy made somewhere else at three in the morning.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*keystore*
*.password
secrets/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- Sibyl local state and generated demo output -------------------------------------
# Both memories, the transaction ledger and the quote. The stores hold this machine's own
# view of two agents; they are rebuildable from chain receipts and are not a build input.
.wrasse/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
policy.json

# --- Foundry --------------------------------------------------------------------------
contracts/cache/
contracts/out/
contracts/broadcast/
contracts/lib/
